title:: BMAbstractSnapShot
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - abstract superclass of automation snapshots
categories:: Classes

Description::

This is the abstract superclass of automation snapshots. Snapshots represent the momentary state of something being automated.

See also: link::Classes/Automation/BMSnapShot::, link::Classes/Automation/BMArbitraryStartSnapShot::, link::Classes/Automation/BMSnapShotSeq::, link::Classes/Automation/BMAbstractAutomator::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMControl::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractController::, link::Overview/Time References and Automation::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Make a new snapshot.

argument:: controls
An Array of Symbols corresponding the names of the BMControl instances to be automated.

argument:: time
Time in seconds for this snapshot. This will be relative to a Time Reference. See Time link::Overview/References and Automation::.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of this snapshot.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: values
Returns an IdentityDictionary in the form of [ctrlname1->value1, ctrlname2->value2, ...] indicating the values of the automated controls at this snapshot's time.

method:: time
Returns the time in seconds for this snapshot. This will be relative to a Time Reference. See link::Overview/Time References and Automation::.

method:: name
Returns a Symbol indicating the name of this snapshot.

method:: controlNames
Returns an Array of Symbols corresponding the names of the BMControl instances being automated.


method:: time
Set the time of this snapshot.

argument:: newTime
The new time in seconds.


method:: isKnown
Returns a Boolean indicating if this snapshot is arbitrary. Arbitrary snapshots are those whose state can only be determined when they become active in an interpolation segment. The default implementation returns true since most snapshots are not arbitrary. Subclasses can override this to return false if need be. See link::Classes/Automation/BMArbitraryStartSnapShot:: for more information.


method:: setValue
Sets the value for a particular control.

argument:: ctrl
A Symbol indicating the name of the control.
argument:: value
The new value, usually a Float.